From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:40:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Find the bundled VAMP plugins from headless tools on Windows

The VAMP plugins shipped with Ardour (libardourvampplugins: EBU R128
loudness, true-peak, ...) are located through VAMP_PATH. On Linux the
wrapper scripts of the command-line tools set VAMP_PATH=@LIBDIR@/vamp,
and on Windows the GUI sets it in fixup_bundle_environment(), but the
headless programs (ardourN-lua, ardourN-export, hardour) have no
wrapper there, so exports from them cannot run the loudness analysis:

  Vamp::HostExt::PluginLoader: No library found in Vamp path for
  plugin "libardourvampplugins:ebur128"

Default VAMP_PATH to <dll-dir>/vamp in ARDOUR::init() on Windows when it
is not already set.
---
 libs/ardour/globals.cc | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/ardour/globals.cc b/libs/ardour/globals.cc
index a54328c..c039143 100644
--- a/libs/ardour/globals.cc
+++ b/libs/ardour/globals.cc
@@ -625,6 +625,19 @@ ARDOUR::init (bool try_optimization, const char* localedir, bool with_gui)
 
 	running_from_gui = with_gui;
 
+#ifdef PLATFORM_WINDOWS
+	/* On Linux the wrapper scripts of the headless tools (ardour-lua,
+	 * ardourN-export, ...) export VAMP_PATH=@LIBDIR@/vamp, and the GUI sets
+	 * it in fixup_bundle_environment(). Windows has no wrapper scripts, so
+	 * point the VAMP host at the bundled plugins (used for export analysis
+	 * and loudness normalization) unless the environment already says
+	 * otherwise.
+	 */
+	if (Glib::getenv ("VAMP_PATH").empty ()) {
+		Glib::setenv ("VAMP_PATH", Glib::build_filename (ardour_dll_directory (), "vamp"), true);
+	}
+#endif
+
 #ifndef NDEBUG
 	if (getenv ("ARDOUR_LUA_METATABLES")) {
 		luabridge::Security::setHideMetatables (false);
